WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.460
Claudia: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:04.320
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.840
between Pringles in Italy and the US.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.507
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.530
Here are all the exclusive flavors

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:16.560
that you will find in Italy
that you won't get in the US.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.060
Here are all the US Pringles

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.320
you're not going to find in Italy.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.570
Starting from paprika.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:23.315
I've got to say paprika
is something that's

00:00:23.315 --> 00:00:25.533
very popular in Spain.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.680
Yeah, it's quite nice, actually.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:31.050
For those who may not
know what paprika is,

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:34.350
it's actually dried, crushed red pepper.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:36.480
Very fruity and fresh, in a way.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.450
I know you guys in the US
have a barbecue flavor.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:42.900
We actually have Texas barbecue.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.120
I don't know, is there
maybe any difference,

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.970
or maybe this is just marketing
to appeal to the Italians

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:51.277
because when you say "Texas barbecue" it

00:00:51.277 --> 00:00:54.013
feels cooler and we
already know what it is?

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:56.880
I don't know. It's barbecue sauce again.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.610
Is barbecue sauce in Texas
supposed to taste different?

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.550
The US actually has dozens
of regional barbecue styles,

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.980
including Texas, which has at least four.

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.270
So it depends on who you ask,

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:08.340
and I don't know where barbecue started.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:10.303
Yeah, we also have just barbecue.

00:01:11.275 --> 00:01:13.410
How do I describe the flavor? Tangy?

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.270
Good, though. I love barbecue.

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:19.143
And then on to the exclusive
train, we've got ketchup.

00:01:20.289 --> 00:01:22.230
Hm. I think it's a bit too strong.

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:23.820
I prefer the other ones.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:26.850
The queen of them all, the pizza flavored.

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:29.880
As I should be, I'm a little
bit worried about those

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:34.170
because as an Italian I'm very
vocal about what pizza is.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:36.870
I have pretty low expectations for these,

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:39.330
just because everything
pizza flavor to me,

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:40.833
it's, like, a bit of a gimmick.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:44.220
No.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:46.250
They just taste like oregano.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:47.880
I don't know why you guys have this idea

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:50.130
that Italians love oregano so much.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:53.456
Like, I have so many spices
and herbs in my kitchen,

00:01:53.456 --> 00:01:55.170
and guess what's missing.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.370
Oregano.

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:59.760
Weirdly, and maybe I'm going
to be canceled for this,

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:03.420
but the ketchup ones
taste more like pizza,

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:05.460
because they taste more like tomatoes.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:07.863
Then we've got smoky bacon.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:12.297
They taste more like the
oil you cook the bacon in.

00:02:12.297 --> 00:02:13.200
Not a fan.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.960
You may also be able to
find Emmental Pringles,

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:18.510
but we were not able to track them down.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:21.390
So, Emmental is a Swiss cheese

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:25.020
made in the German part of Switzerland.

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:27.360
Oh, cheddar cheese. Let's go!

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.533
Bursting with flavor.

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:31.110
Get that on screen.

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:31.943
Good.

00:02:31.943 --> 00:02:34.740
Ooh, I've never had this
one before, hot honey.

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:35.573
Nope.

00:02:35.573 --> 00:02:38.313
Ah, cheddar and sour cream.
Dude, these are always good.

00:02:39.462 --> 00:02:41.220
Mm! The chive!

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:42.270
Salt and vinegar.

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:43.500
Got ranch.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:46.470
Not the best ranch-flavored
chip out there, but not bad.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:47.940
I think Claudia should try these.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:49.359
Yo, Claudia, catch!

00:02:49.359 --> 00:02:50.309
Gah!

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:55.890
Thanks, Joe.

00:02:55.890 --> 00:03:00.033
I've actually never had ranch
sauce or, like, dressing.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:03.960
I can already see people
sort of walking away from me

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:05.430
the moment I start talking to them

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:07.878
because of the onion.

00:03:07.878 --> 00:03:09.809
It's very potent.

00:03:09.809 --> 00:03:11.040
No.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.657
I'm seeing flames on both of
these. I'm seeing a grill.

00:03:13.657 --> 00:03:16.080
So assumption is these are spicy.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.846
Enchilada adobada.

00:03:18.846 --> 00:03:21.777
And the las meras meras habaneras.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:24.360
Not a lot of heat to
them, but pretty good.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:26.220
I don't know if that tastes
like an enchilada, but.

00:03:27.585 --> 00:03:29.226
Mm!

00:03:29.226 --> 00:03:31.260
These are good. They're not like Takis,

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:32.940
but they're in the Taki
space. They're spicy.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:35.377
They have a Flamin' Hot
Cheeto kind of vibe to it.

00:03:35.377 --> 00:03:37.233
Minecraft suspicious stew.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.508
Limited time only. Thank God.

00:03:40.508 --> 00:03:42.660
Look, he's got a little
gamer headset on there.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:46.143
Shameless, Julius Pringle.
Shameless, going after the kids.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:48.570
I'm surprised. For
something that's clearly

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:49.403
marketed as kids,

00:03:49.403 --> 00:03:52.230
this does not have a
very strong flavor to it.

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:54.030
Tastes like a weak sour cream and onion.

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:55.050
Philly cheesesteak.

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:57.480
Check out the best
cheesesteak in Philadelphia

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:00.330
"Food Tours" episode,
staring myself and Harry.

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:04.050
And this is that sandwich in chip form.

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:06.663
I can't imagine one
human being wanting this.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:10.800
Avoid this.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:11.940
Oh, smells terrible.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:13.800
There's also a French fries and ketchup

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.600
and everything bagel flavor

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.280
we were not able to get for this shoot.

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:19.007
Let's get scorched.

00:04:19.007 --> 00:04:21.090
We also have a line of scorchin',

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:23.490
I-N-apostrophe, Pringles.

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:26.820
You can see the steam
coming out of Julius' ears.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:28.440
This one, he's crying.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:29.970
He's crying on the Buffalo one.

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:32.085
He's not crying on the other ones. OK.

00:04:32.085 --> 00:04:33.060
Something to look forward to.

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:34.660
Start down here with the barbecue.

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:37.740
Come on!

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:38.673
Get hot!

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:40.950
Nope, not scorchin'.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:42.636
Let's try the cheddar.

00:04:42.636 --> 00:04:45.150
I mean, they even have the
temperature thing in the logo.

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:47.073
The thermometer going up.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:49.470
Not only are they not scorchin',

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:52.050
but also I'm not really
getting any flavor. Cheddar?

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:53.100
Sour cream and onion.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:56.600
I mean, I love sour cream
and onion chips. [coughs]

00:04:57.866 --> 00:04:58.699
Mm.

00:04:58.699 --> 00:05:00.180
They taste like sour cream
and onion chips, but,

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:02.640
I mean, I'm getting a little,
like, low-level spice.

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:05.469
This one, as you can see,
Julius Pringle is crying.

00:05:05.469 --> 00:05:07.230
Look at this. The chip, the pepper,

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:09.680
and the bottle of hot
sauce are all on fire.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.201
Little bit of heat. Yeah, there it is!

00:05:13.201 --> 00:05:15.495
There it is! OK.

00:05:15.495 --> 00:05:18.270
I guess look for the tears
if you want spicy Pringles.

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:19.353
Chili and lime.

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:21.263
No.

00:05:21.263 --> 00:05:22.890
Instead of scorchin', in Italy,

00:05:22.890 --> 00:05:25.410
spicy Pringles are called flame,

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:28.710
and you can find them
as a spicy BBQ flavor

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:30.783
and cheese and chili flavor.

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:34.110
I think I'll be able to have a few

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:36.150
without having to go and drink,

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:37.440
but I think it's manageable.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.060
It's a very manageable spice.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:41.190
Let's try the cheese and chili now.

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:43.320
This one have two chilies on them,

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:47.340
so they're supposed to
be the mild-ish ones,

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:49.323
whereas these have three.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.590
Ooh!

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:56.070
You're attacked by this cheese
taste, cheese flavoring,

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:57.636
fake-cheese taste.

00:05:57.636 --> 00:05:58.794
Not nice.

00:05:58.794 --> 00:06:00.660
Also in the US you can
get something called

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:03.240
the Pringles harvest blend.

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:05.100
Four varieties to choose from.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:07.207
According to the ad copy,

00:06:07.207 --> 00:06:10.020
"A deliciously complex tasting experience

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:12.043
unlike one you've ever had."

00:06:12.043 --> 00:06:13.560
Barf!

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:14.580
They're potato chips.

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:18.483
Let's embark on this taste
journey unlike any other.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:20.753
Hang on.

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:24.300
The taste difference between these two

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:26.130
are hardly noticeable.

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:28.020
They definitely look different.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.220
Homestyle ranch.

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:30.540
Also multigrain.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:33.270
Amazon. This guy drop-kicked
this to my front door.

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:34.563
This is ridiculous!

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:37.230
These are different than
their regular ranch,

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:38.470
and I do like these.

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:42.195
Flavor's not as strong, not
as insane, which I like.

00:06:42.195 --> 00:06:44.311
Sweet potatoes, next are sweet potato,

00:06:44.311 --> 00:06:45.630
and this is sea salt.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:47.403
I like that. I like sweet potatoes,

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.550
I like maracas, so.

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:52.833
OK, again, the sweet
potato smoky barbecue.

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:56.160
I've definitely experienced this before,

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:58.020
so I want to update that ad copy.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:00.810
The last exclusives we have
is the lighter side range,

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:02.400
where you can get the lightly salted

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:04.230
and the reduced-fat original.

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:06.120
Could not get them for
the time of filming,

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:07.596
and honestly, I'm glad.

00:07:07.596 --> 00:07:10.113
I'm not interested in less
salt or less fat. Forget it.

00:07:10.113 --> 00:07:13.110
So, if I were to rank them all, let's see.

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:14.433
OK, worst, pizza.

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:16.713
Didn't like the bacon.

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:19.980
Didn't like this one with the cheese.

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:21.450
Let's put the other spicy one,

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:24.210
just because I'm not so big on spices.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:25.890
Now I'm going to put the ketchup.

00:07:25.890 --> 00:07:27.690
I'm going to put this one here,

00:07:27.690 --> 00:07:29.580
and probably the paprika

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:32.490
is the one that I will reach out for.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:33.810
OK, in no particular order,

00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:35.580
my favorites of the day were

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:37.830
the las meras meras habaneras.

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:39.330
Very good. Taking these home.

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:41.010
Cheddar and sour cream.

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:42.180
Always good.

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:43.650
Scorchin' series, a little disappointed

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:45.870
except for the Buffalo.
My guy's crying on there,

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:47.760
so you know that they're scorching.

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:49.320
And I did like the harvest blend ones,

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:50.490
the sweet potato ones.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:51.780
I sign off on them.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:52.680
Here's what sucked.

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:55.096
Hot honey. Not hot, very little honey.

00:07:55.096 --> 00:07:57.030
The Philly cheesesteak
thing. Yeah, you can't.

00:07:57.030 --> 00:07:58.980
And this Minecraft suspicious stew.

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:00.810
I don't, I'm not eating
anything called "suspicious,"

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:01.793
that's just weird.

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:06.480
In Italy, our Pringles come in four sizes.

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:09.240
We've got a 40-gram small size.

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:13.620
You may also be able to find
a pop-and-go 70-grams tube,

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:15.930
but we were not able to track it down.

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:17.513
And then you can also get them

00:08:17.513 --> 00:08:20.970
in the 175-grams standard tube.

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:24.570
But if you get the flame
spicy Pringle range,

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:28.440
you only get for the
standard tube 160 grams,

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.990
even though the tubes
look exactly the same.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:32.640
Maybe it's done to protect you.

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:35.790
Sometimes Pringles releases a 3-foot tube,

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:39.510
which always breaks the internet
when it actually comes out.

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:42.030
Sadly, it was not in stores right now,

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:44.370
but it looks like it's just three tubes

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:46.020
stacked on top of one another.

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:48.933
So visually, this is what you will get.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:53.550
Here in the US, our
Pringles come in five sizes.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:56.008
Snack stack, then another little one,

00:08:56.008 --> 00:08:58.650
the grab-and-go, the original tube,

00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:00.570
and the party stack.

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:04.320
That means that the biggest
American size is 10% larger

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:06.720
than the biggest Italian one.

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:09.480
We wanted to find out how
many Pringles are in a tube,

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:12.120
but we didn't really want
to count them one by one.

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:15.030
So we're going to weigh
them and do some maths.

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:19.290
We should be getting 87.5
Pringles in each tube.

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:21.480
Well, the 0.5 is maybe
some, like, crumbles.

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:23.640
The numbers, as we have crunched here

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:25.680
at the "Food Wars" math lab,

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:27.750
is 149 grams total.

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:30.420
And if one chip is 1.9 grams,

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:31.860
that equals

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:36.031
78.4 chips on average per tube.

00:09:38.078 --> 00:09:41.511
In Italy, the original
Pringles contain the following.

00:09:41.511 --> 00:09:44.970
The original Pringles in
the US contain all of this.

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:47.250
There aren't any major differences,

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:48.900
except for actually coloring

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:51.390
that we do add to our
Pringles here in Italy.

00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:54.550
It's annatto. It's made from plants,

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:56.160
and it's totally natural.

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:59.100
I mean, annatto is very dark.

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:01.140
It's a flashy orangey brown.

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:03.900
So it's still very far from this coloring,

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:06.570
but there is a difference with the US.

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:08.640
The longest ingredient list for Pringles

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:09.870
in the US are these,

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:12.060
the scorchin' sour cream and onion,

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:15.150
with 47 ingredients. Good God!

00:10:15.150 --> 00:10:16.590
Eleven of these are main ingredients,

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:18.720
and 36 are subingredients.

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:21.030
Now, many of these are flavoring spices

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:24.246
and different dairy products
to create the cream flavor

00:10:24.246 --> 00:10:25.110
as well as some colorings

00:10:25.110 --> 00:10:26.670
which you may not have heard of before.

00:10:26.670 --> 00:10:29.340
Red 40, yellow 5, and yellow 6.

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:31.050
There's new evidence that red 40

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:34.320
is triggering inflammatory bowel disease

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:38.040
because it is disrupting the
way the gut barrier works,

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:41.310
which is harmful and
encourages inflammation.

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:42.870
First it scorches your tongue,

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:44.760
and then it scorches your bowels.

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:46.382
UK manufacturers

00:10:46.382 --> 00:10:48.323
were made to remove this
from their products.

00:10:48.323 --> 00:10:51.450
However, it can be
legally sold by EU imports

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:53.857
providing it is properly labeled,

00:10:53.857 --> 00:10:56.340
"May have an adverse effect on activity

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:57.660
and attention in children."

00:10:57.660 --> 00:11:00.120
Yellow No. 5, also called tartrazine,

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:01.500
is a type of sodium salt

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:05.460
that, when eaten, it
becomes "sulfanic" acid?

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:07.770
It is this acid that can
cause allergic reactions,

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:11.190
especially in asthmatic
people, and can produce eczema,

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:13.620
hives, and also hyperactivity in children.

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:15.810
Many Nordic countries have banned its use,

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:17.790
but it is approved in the US and UK.

00:11:17.790 --> 00:11:18.840
Heads up, Harry.

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:23.340
Yellow No. 6, also called
sunset yellow or E110,

00:11:23.340 --> 00:11:24.630
is similar to tartrazine.

00:11:24.630 --> 00:11:27.060
And these colors have appeared
in a bunch of flavors,

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:28.360
these specifically.

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:33.390
Obviously Pringles is a very
well-known brand in Italy,

00:11:33.390 --> 00:11:37.350
but I think the idea of chips as a thing,

00:11:37.350 --> 00:11:40.080
for us, chips are not
really a thing of their own.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:42.630
They're, like, part of a family of snacks.

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:45.180
In Italy, we tend to have chips

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:47.970
on a snack board with other things,

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:49.560
other items like olives

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:52.140
or tiny pieces of focaccia.

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:55.920
Pringles is not the first brand
that I would reach out to.

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:59.850
It's funny because to me all
these seem quite a big number.

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:01.500
Having to decide between, like,

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:02.825
three, four, five, six, seven,

00:12:02.825 --> 00:12:04.980
seven flavors,

00:12:04.980 --> 00:12:08.220
and then you got the original, it's a lot.

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:11.640
We just saw the 500
different flavors they have.

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:14.575
Pringles, they're doing
every flavor. Good for them.

00:12:14.575 --> 00:12:16.110
But as far as the classics,

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:18.300
the salt and vinegar, the
barbecue, the cheddar,

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:19.525
sour cream and onion,

00:12:19.525 --> 00:12:21.390
I feel like Pringles is pretty good at

00:12:21.390 --> 00:12:22.530
doing most flavors.

00:12:22.530 --> 00:12:24.088
But they also had that
stupid Minecraft flavor,

00:12:24.088 --> 00:12:25.313
so I don't know.

00:12:25.313 --> 00:12:27.540
I don't know. They are
exclusive to the Italian market,

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:31.740
but they still do seem
adapted to the Italian market,

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:34.410
versus created for the Italian market.

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:36.660
If you wanted something very Italian,

00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:38.820
you should have put an olive oil one.

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:40.860
You're really missing an opportunity here.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:43.500
Just put an olive-oil-flavored chip.

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:45.270
We've talked about this
on "Food Wars" before.

00:12:45.270 --> 00:12:48.090
In America, chips and snacks
are all going after each other.

00:12:48.090 --> 00:12:49.980
They might be owned by the same company,

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:51.600
and they're just, like, cross-pollinating,

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:53.880
but the chip aisle is just all filled with

00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:56.220
these different iterations
of the same kind of idea, so,

00:12:56.220 --> 00:12:57.690
I see tube snacks all the time.

00:12:57.690 --> 00:13:00.570
I've got actually here some
of the most popular ones.

00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:03.600
We've got Fonzies, which are like,

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:05.130
pretty much like chips.

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:08.700
You know, in a way, this is a
very traditional Italian chip.

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:10.239
You also find these.

00:13:10.239 --> 00:13:12.120
These are called crostini.

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:13.680
This is like dried bread, you know?

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:16.730
It's a bit like crumbs.
As you say, like crouton.

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:19.800
Especially in the south of
Italy where I'm from, Bari,

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:21.480
we make these all the time.

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:22.710
They're called taralli.

00:13:22.710 --> 00:13:23.730
Shape is always the same,

00:13:23.730 --> 00:13:25.740
but you always get them
in different flavors.

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:27.420
Actually, my grandma makes them,

00:13:27.420 --> 00:13:29.580
and it's, like, the best thing ever.

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:32.730
And they're made with
flour, olive oil, and wine.

00:13:32.730 --> 00:13:37.143
So this is the absolute OG Italian snack.

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:39.983
The best.

00:13:39.983 --> 00:13:42.775
My grandma's are better, but this is good.

